  "ingredients": [
    "3 tablespoon avocado oil",
    "1 medium yellow onion (diced)",
    "4 medium celery (diced)",
    "2 whole bay leaf",
    "1 1/2 teaspoon fresh oregano",
    "16 ounce boneless, skinless chicken thighs",
    "1/2 cup pumpkin puree",
    "1 cup chicken broth",
    "6 ounce green olive (pitted)",
    "1 medium lemon (juice of)",
    "6 tablespoon butter",
    "24 ounce cauliflower",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out and prepare all the ingredients. Heat an Instant Pot or pressure cooker on saute mode.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/garden-chicken-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the Instant Pot or pressure cooker, add avocado oil, diced celery, onion, and bay leaf. Saute until everything is tender.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Garden-Chicken-with-Cauliflower-Rice-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the oregano and chicken, then season with salt and pepper. Cook for about 5 minutes uncovered or until the chicken is browned on both sides.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/garden-chicken-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the pumpkin puree, chicken broth, and pitted green olives. Stir well. Turn the pressure cooker on high, close the lid, and set to cook for 25 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Garden-Chicken-with-Cauliflower-Rice-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the meantime, make the cauliflower rice. Rice the cauliflower using a food processor - pulse florets of cauliflower until they resemble small crumbles. Work in batches if needed. In a pan over medium heat, melt the butter and add the riced cauliflower. Cook this for 8-10 minutes. Season with salt and pepper to taste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Garden-Chicken-with-Cauliflower-Rice-5.png"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once pressure has released, open the lid and shred the chicken.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Garden-Chicken-with-Cauliflower-Rice-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Put the shredded chicken back into the pot and squeeze the lemon into it. Stir well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Garden-Chicken-with-Cauliflower-Rice-7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve the chicken with cauliflower rice. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/garden-chicken-with-cauliflower-rice/#wprm-recipe-53677-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
